#: ../../../HowToSetUpLLVMStyleRTTI.md:224
msgid ""
"Note that this is the reason that we did not need to introduce a `classof` "
"into `Shape`: all relevant classes derive from `Shape`, and `Shape` itself "
"is abstract (has no entry in the `Kind` enum), so this notional inferred "
"`classof` is all we need. See [Concrete Bases and Deeper Hierarchies]"
"(#concrete-bases-and-deeper-hierarchies) for more information about how to "
"extend this example to more general hierarchies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToSetUpLLVMStyleRTTI.md:231
msgid ""
"Although for this small example setting up LLVM-style RTTI seems like a lot "
"of \"boilerplate\", if your classes are doing anything interesting then this "
"will end up being a tiny fraction of the code."
msgstr ""

